word is fixed and permanent: it is never rotated and grants the `pki-admin` role, including non-interactive tokens through the `frontend` client"},"178":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-75/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-100","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-75/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-75/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#development-mode","content":"the `frontend` client accepts any redirect URI and any web origin (`*`) instead of the original `/*` patterns"},"179":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-75/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-101","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-75/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-75/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#development-mode","content":"With `--development`, the fixed `lamassu`/`lamassu` password grants `pki-admin` access to anyone who can reach the installation. Never use it on anything exposed beyond a development machine or a network-reachable host."},"180":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-75/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-102","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-75/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-75/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#development-mode","content":"`--development` applies when the `lamassu` realm is first imported. It does not modify an existing cluster. It can be combined with `--sample-data`: the development transform runs first, then sample data is added to the same realm configuration."},"181":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-75/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-103","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-75/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-75/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#what-the-script-configures","content":"Fastlane:"},"182":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-75/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane-104","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-75/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-75/deployment/self-hosted/fastlane#wha