ne principal's policy with an attribute belonging to another."],[543,"HTTP rules"],[640,"HTTP rules do not point directly at tables. They reference a route schema and grant its logical actions. Job Manager's policies are an example: they distinguish reading, creating, updating and deleting workflows or jobs."],[583,"HTTP rules primarily answer &#x2A;*\"can this identity call this API operation?\"**. On their own they do not produce filters over the external service's database. To limit a route to a specific device, tenant or client, either the schema declares a constraint relating a request value to a normalized attribute of the principal, or the policy pins the request value to a literal with `param_constraints`. The first scopes each identity to its own resources through a single grant; the second restricts a grant to a fixed value regardless of who holds it."],[1431,"HTTP URL of Lamassu's CA service."],[1427,"HTTP URL of Lamassu's Device Manager."],[1423,"HTTP URL of Lamassu's DMS Manager service."],[418,"I cannot sign in"],[1355,"IAM action"],[1437,"IAM actions"],[1708,"ID created automatically and correct DMS."],[2207,"ID of the CA the settings belong to."],[968,"ID of the signing CA."],[1164,"ID, owning DMS, certificate CN and bound serial."],[2087,"Identify a certificate by issuer and serial; a name can correspond to several renewals. Check which certificate the consumer actually uses and which occupies the device’s active identity. Identity history and the certificate inventory answer different questions."],[2137,"Identify DMSs, devices and services that trust that chain."],[2553,"Identify the certificate"],[1956,"Identify the certificates, devices and consumers that depend on the CA. Prepare a replacement authority and chain when necessary."],[937,"Identify the fleet"],[777,"Identify the operation"],[379,"Identity"],[2040,"Identity"],[2156,"Identity flow"],[469,"If `amqp.tls` is enabled, verify the TLS side as well:"],[3006,"If `kms` has not been migrated, 